# The skips a suite run with the embedder SWITCHED OFF (-Djawata.embed.disabled=true)
# is expected to make, on top of its platform's own budget. Used by CI's embedder-off job
# as `abort-budget.sh <log> linux,embedder-off`. One pattern per line; a line is matched
# as a substring of the abort message.
#
# --- REL44-24 (Sprint 28g), 2026-10-15 ---
# Why the job exists: no gate ran ANY test with the embedder off, so a test that FAILS
# without an embedder - rather than skipping - was invisible on every machine that has
# one, which is every machine this project builds on. Running nine classes that way turned
# up two such tests and one assertion hidden behind an if (REL44-21). The degrade path the
# product promises - a broken embedder leaves the product working exactly as before - was
# exercised only by the few tests that switch it off themselves.
#
# Why these skips are acceptable: a test whose subject IS meaning recall cannot run without
# the model, and says so instead of passing. Every such assumption in the suite words its
# reason one of these two ways; a skip worded otherwise fails the budget, which is the
# point - a new skip is a decision, read before it is accepted.
no embedder
embedder unavailable
